Port B on the M5Stack Core2 exposes GPIO36 and GPIO26, which are used here as the clock (SCK) and data (DOUT) lines for the HX711's bit-banged digital protocol — note that GPIO36 is input-only on the ESP32, so GPIO26 is assigned to the output clock line.

**Wiring Table**

| Component Pin | Connects to M5Stack Core2 |
|---|---|
| VCC | 3.3V (Grove Port B) |
| GND | GND (Grove Port B) |
| DOUT | GPIO36 (Port B pin1) |
| SCK | GPIO26 (Port B pin2) |

**Wiring Diagram**
```
+---------------------+          +------------------+
|    M5Stack Core2    |          |      HX711       |
|                     |          |                  |
|  Port B (Grove)     |          |                  |
|  GPIO36 (pin1) -----+----------+ DOUT             |
|  GPIO26 (pin2) -----+----------+ SCK              |
|  3.3V          -----+----------+ VCC              |
|  GND           -----+----------+ GND              |
+---------------------+          |                  |
